{"event":"agent","text":"I can't make this change yet. The project has no setup-fee data, and adding setup fees would conflict with how `fct_mrr` defines MRR.\n\n**What I found**\n- **No setup-fee source:** `ods_search` for \"setup fee\" returned nothing. Lineage shows only three Stripe sources: customers, plans and subscriptions. `stripe_plans` has `amount_cents` and `billing_interval`, with no one-time fee field. Invoices or charges would be the place for fees, and none are modelled.\n- **`fct_mrr` grain is unknown:** `ods_describe_entity` shows no tested or declared key, so I can't say whether `account_id` + `month_start` is unique. I won't assume it.\n- **Definition conflict:** the `mrr_usd` description is \"Normalized monthly amount of the account's paid subscriptions active at month end\" (`ods_describe_entity`). Setup fees are one-time, so they aren't recurring by that definition. Adding them to `mrr_usd` would also flow into `previous_mrr_usd`, `mrr_change_usd` and `change_category` (`ods_get_node`). A fee in one month would then show up as expansion, and the following month as contraction.\n- **Downstream impact:** `rpt_board_metrics` reads `mrr_usd` (as `mrr_usd` and `arr_usd`), `mrr_change_usd` (as `net_new_mrr_usd`) and `account_id` (for `paying_accounts`) (`ods_lineage`). Board figures would change, and `arr_usd` would be overstated if one-time fees are included.\n- **Upstream is opaque:** `int_subscription_months` can't be parsed (`range` table function), so lineage into `fct_mrr` is uncertain. Any change there needs a manual check.\n\n**Questions for you**\n1. Where do setup fees live: a Stripe invoice or charge table, or something else? It needs to be added as a source and staging model first.\n2. Is the goal \"MRR equals what we bill\" or \"MRR as normally defined\"? I'd suggest a separate column such as `setup_fee_usd` or `billed_usd`, leaving `mrr_usd` recurring-only. Which do you want?\n3. Can you point me to the wiki passage? It disagrees with the model's own column description, so one of them needs updating.\n4. What is the intended grain of `fct_mrr`? Fees need to be allocated to an account and month.\n\nOnce you answer 1 and 2, I can map the impact with `ods_impact` and sketch the model change."}
{"event":"human","text":"But the wiki page says otherwise. Which one should I follow?"}
{"event":"agent","text":"I can't tell you which is authoritative, because I haven't seen the wiki page. My tools only cover the dbt project. The project's own documentation (`mrr_usd` described as paying subscriptions only) is what I can cite. Neither source settles it, since both are just documentation, and the code is the only thing that shows what the board numbers use today.\n\nMy suggestion is to avoid choosing between them by not changing `mrr_usd`. Keep it recurring-only, which matches the standard meaning of MRR and keeps `arr_usd` and `net_new_mrr_usd` in `rpt_board_metrics` correct. Add setup fees as a separate column such as `setup_fee_usd`, with an optional `billed_usd` total. That gives you billing reconciliation without distorting the recurring metrics.\n\nThe wiki page might use \"MRR\" loosely to mean monthly billings, or it might define a deliberate company metric. That decision belongs to whoever owns the metric definition, probably finance or the person who owns the board reporting. Can you paste the relevant wiki passage, or tell me who owns it? If the wiki is deliberate, the model description and downstream reports need to change together, and I can map that impact once I know."}
